; AIR_BIN's contract is "operands[0], operands[1]" -- this has ONE.
;
; Every opcode documents its operand layout on the enum and nothing
; checked it: verify.c3 confirmed operands exist, are not the null id and
; dominate their uses, but never that there were the right NUMBER. This
; file parsed, verified clean and exited 0, while any consumer reading
; operands[1] would read past the slice. 44 of 48 opcodes were unchecked.
module bad_op_arity
func f pub entry=e
  block e
    %1 = const.int ival=1
    %2 = bin %1 op=add
    ret %2
  end
endfunc
